summary: Upload the artifact-server qcow2 to AWS as an AMI

description: |
    Run the upstream testing-farm/tests ``/testing-farm/upload-qcow2`` test
    (``tft-admin``, inside the cnc image) on the qcow2 produced by a
    ``/image-mode/qcow2/build`` request.

    The prepare step derives QCOW2_URL from QCOW2_REQUEST inside Testing Farm,
    where the Red Hat ranch artifact server is reachable (the GitLab runner cannot
    resolve it), and hands it to the test through the plan environment.

    Required variables:

      QCOW2_REQUEST ... The /image-mode/qcow2/build request id. Ignored if
                        QCOW2_URL is set.

      IMAGE_NAME    ... Image name under which it is stored in the cloud.

      QCOW2_ARCH    ... Arch of the qcow2, passed to tft-admin.

    Optional variables:

      QCOW2_URL         ... Download URL of the qcow2, skips the derivation.

      QCOW2_FILE        ... Name of the qcow2 file, default artifacts-bootc.qcow2.

      REMOVE_AFTER_TEST ... When set, delete the uploaded image after the upload.
                            Only the us-east-1 copy is removed.

    Secret variables:

      VAULT_SECRET_ID ... Hashicorp Vault secret id for the cnc container. Pass as a
                          Testing Farm secret (``-s``).

environment:
  CLOUD: arr-aws
  QCOW2_FILE: artifacts-bootc.qcow2

discover:
  how: fmf
  url: https://gitlab.com/testing-farm/tests
  test:
    - /testing-farm/upload-qcow2

provision:
  how: container
  image: quay.io/testing-farm/cnc:latest
  user: cnc

prepare:
  - name: Derive the qcow2 URL
    how: shell
    script: |
      set -euo pipefail
      if [ -z "${QCOW2_URL:-}" ]; then
        url=$(python3 "$TMT_TREE/images/artifacts/qcow2-url.py" "${QCOW2_REQUEST:?QCOW2_REQUEST or QCOW2_URL must be set}")
        echo "QCOW2_URL=$url" >> "$TMT_PLAN_ENVIRONMENT_FILE"
      fi

execute:
  how: tmt
